Replace the FDE cryptfs functions that vold 14.1 no longer provides.

Runs 39179952900 and 39185450564 failed on undeclared
cryptfs_get_password_type and cryptfs_check_passwd (partitionmanager.cpp)
and delete_crypto_blk_dev (partition.cpp); partition.cpp also calls
set_partition_data and cryptfs_check_footer. vold 14.1 (like AOSP since
Android 13) has no FDE, so cryptfs.h only declares the ext-volume
helpers. This adds twrp_fde_compat.h, included next to cryptfs.h:
- the FDE-only calls fail, since FBE devices with a keydirectory such
  as rothko never take those paths;
- delete_crypto_blk_dev does the DM_DEV_REMOVE ioctl the old TWRP
  cryptfs did, because Format Data (Wipe_Encryption) uses it to drop
  the metadata-encryption "userdata" dm device before formatting.
Applies after 0002.

